The four flips are independent and fair, so the $16$ sequences of heads and tails are equally likely.

Exactly four heads is $1$ sequence. Exactly three heads is $4$ sequences, since any one of the four positions can hold the single tail. So $5$ sequences have at least three heads.

P(\text{four heads} \mid \text{at least three heads}) = \frac{1}{5}
